      "writtenOn": "2022-10-14T16:50:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The vhost-user is a mechanism to run device emulation in a separate process. So, we need to make sure the frontend (the vmm side) and the backend (the device side) use the same queue sizes.\n\nAs for Noah\u0027s concern, I guess this CL is fine because we don\u0027t allow changing queue sizes for vhost-user. This line is for the front-end and [this](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/crosvm/+/refs/changes/55/2197155/5/devices/src/virtio/vhost/user/device/block.rs#142) is for the back-end. As far as we\u0027re using the same constant value at this two places, I think vhost-user should work.\n\nI think we should use the same `DEFAULT_NUM_QUEUES` in the backend implementation, but we don\u0027t need to do it in this CL.\nNoah, does it make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "a6137351_91d1a611",
